visualize what's going on,

04:33.795 --> 04:35.165
you'll say well okay
look they're just taking

04:35.165 --> 04:38.370
point V and they're
rotating it by 137 degrees

04:38.370 --> 04:40.204
around point O.

04:40.204 --> 04:43.594
And so this would be a rotation.

04:43.594 --> 04:45.761
Let's do one more example.

04:47.100 --> 04:49.237
So here we are told,

04:49.237 --> 04:50.305
so they're talking about,

04:50.305 --> 04:53.881
again a certain mapping in the xy-plane.

04:53.881 --> 04:56.226
Each circle O with radius r

04:56.226 --> 04:58.966
and centered at x y is
mapped to a circle O'

04:58.966 --> 05:01.961
with radius r and centered at x plus 11

05:01.961 --> 05:03.878
and then y minus seven.

05:05.050 --> 05:06.930
So once again pause this
video, what is this?

05:06.930 --> 05:09.183
Reflection, rotation, or translation?

05:09.183 --> 05:11.667
All right so you might be tempted,

05:11.667 --> 05:13.037
