05:14.291 --> 05:15.499
maybe they're talking about a rotation.

05:15.499 --> 05:17.449
But look, what they're really saying is,

05:17.449 --> 05:20.073
is that if I have a circle,

05:20.073 --> 05:22.557
let's say I have a circle right over here,

05:22.557 --> 05:24.392
centered right over here.

05:24.392 --> 05:26.969
After it, so this is x comma y,

05:26.969 --> 05:28.455
centered at x comma y.

05:28.455 --> 05:32.287
It's mapped to a new circle
O' with the same radius.

05:32.287 --> 05:34.191
So if this is the radius,

05:34.191 --> 05:36.629
it's mapped to a new circle
with the same radius,

05:36.629 --> 05:38.796
but now it is centered at,

05:40.228 --> 05:43.432
now it is centered at x plus 11,

05:43.432 --> 05:46.149
so our new x-coordinate
is gonna be 11 larger,

05:46.149 --> 05:50.166
x plus 11, and our y-coordinate
is gonna be seven less.

05:50.166 --> 05:52.627
But we have the exact same radius.

05:52.627 --> 05:54.926
We have the exact same radius.

05:54.926 --> 05:57.062
So our circle would still,

05:57.062 --> 05:59.361
so we have the exact same
radius right over here.

05:59.361 --> 06:02.356
So what just happened to the circle?

06:02.356 --> 06:04.144
Well we kept the radius the same,

06:04.144 --> 06:05.955
and we just shifted,

06:05.955 --> 06:08.649
we just shifted our center

06:08.649 --> 06:10.832
to the right by 11,

06:10.832 --> 06:14.249
plus 11, and we shifted it down by seven.

06:15.592 --> 06:17.565
We shifted it down by seven.

06:17.565 --> 06:20.259
So this is clearly a translation.

06:20.259 --> 06:22.697
So we would select that right over there.

06:22.697 --> 06:23.947
And we're done.
